+/**
+* How long the mux WebSocket may go without answering a ping before it is
+* terminated.
+*
+* Two seconds is short enough to matter on a slow link. The ping is queued
+* behind whatever the server is pushing, and the server pushes megabytes of
+* events to a client that is reaching it over a tunnel; the client does not
+* see the ping until that data has arrived, and its pong has to make one
+* more round trip. A socket that misses two pongs is therefore terminated
+* while it is still being filled — and every termination makes the client
+* re-read the model catalog and the whole Session list, which is what made
